  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.046,
            0.363,
            0.062
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.367,
            0.106
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_1.jpg",
          "content": "(4 + 3) \\times 5 = 7 \\times 5 = 35"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.116,
            0.587,
            0.139
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5 × 4 + 3 ≠ 5 × (4 + 3). Can you explain why?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.147,
            0.52,
            0.166
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{I} \\mathrm{s} 5 \\times (4+3)=5 \\times (3+4)=(3+4) \\times 5?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.178,
            0.846,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The observations that we have made in the previous two examples can be seen in a general way as follows."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.215,
            0.848,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10 \\times 98 + 3 \\times 98"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This means taking the sum of 10 times 98 and 3 times 98."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.257,
            0.797,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.188,
                0.257,
                0.797,
                0.322
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.333,
            0.7,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Clearly, this is the same as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10+3=13"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " times 98. Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.357,
            0.647,
            0.376
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "10 \\times 98 + 3 \\times 98 = (10 + 3) \\times 98."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.382,
            0.604,
            0.402
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Writing this equality the other way, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.406,
            0.641,
            0.425
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "(10 + 3)\\;98 = 10 \\times 98 \\pm 3 \\times 98."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.43,
            0.847,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Swapping the numbers in the products above, this property can be seen in the following form:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.335,
            0.472,
            0.664,
            0.492
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "98 \\times 10 + 9 \\times 83 = 98(10 + 3)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.356,
            0.502,
            0.642,
            0.521
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "98\\left (10 \\div 3\\right ) = 98 \\times 10 + 98 \\times 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.526,
            0.847,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, let us consider the expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "14 \\times 10 - 6 \\times 10"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . This means subtracting 6 times 10 from 14 times 10."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.458,
            0.576,
            0.536,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14 times"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.574,
            0.814,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.182,
                0.574,
                0.814,
                0.637
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_16.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.647,
            0.567,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Clearly, this is 14 – 6 = 8 times 10. Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.347,
            0.672,
            0.651,
            0.715
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{14 \\times 10 - 6 \\times 10}_{ \\text{000000000}} &= (14 - 6) \\times 10, \\\\  or  \\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.352,
            0.72,
            0.647,
            0.739
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "(14 - 6) \\times 10 = 14 \\times 10 - 6 \\times 10"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.744,
            0.682,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This property can be nicely summed up as follows:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.768,
            0.847,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The multiple of a sum (difference) is the same as the sum (difference) of the multiples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.825,
            0.396,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Tinker the Terms II"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.856,
            0.848,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us understand what happens when we change the numbers occurring in a product."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.938,
            0.188,
            0.953
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "40"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
